.TH ISO2CHD 1 "September 2026" "2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iso2chd \- Advanced Batch ISO/BIN to CHD conversion utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iso2chd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGETS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iso2chd
is a robust command-line utility designed to batch convert standard disk images (.iso, .bin/.cue) into Compressed Hunks of Data (.chd) using MAME's chdman tool. It supports recursive directory scanning, custom multi-threading, custom compression codecs, and storage savings telemetry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-recursive\fR
Scan subdirectories recursively for disk images when targeting directories.
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep\fR
Keep source disk images after a successful conversion.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mode\fR <\fImode\fR>
Specify conversion mode: \fIauto\fR, \fIdvd\fR (createdvd), or \fIcd\fR (createcd).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-codec\fR <\fIcodec\fR>
Compression codec to apply (e.g., \fIzlib\fR, \fIlzma\fR, \fIhuff\fR).
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR <\fInum\fR>
Number of processor threads to utilize during compression.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verify\fR
Verify CHD file integrity right after creation via chdman verify.
.TP
\fB\-\-info\fR <\fIfile\fR>
Inspect internal headers and metadata of an existing CHD file using chdman info.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help text and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.SH AUTHOR
